    "title": "When Will NASA’s Artemis II Mission Reach the Moon? - The New York Times",
    "text": "AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENT See more of our coverage in your search results.Encuentra más de nuestra cobertura en los resultados de búsqueda. Add The New York Times on GoogleAgrega The New York Times en Google After a picture-perfect launch on Wednesday evening, Artemis II is one step closer to the moon. If the mission continues as planned, the Orion capsule will reach the moon in five days, by Monday night.The spacecraft will orbit 43,730 miles above Earth’s surface for about 24 hours on what NASA calls a high-Earth orbit. This wide, looping path provides time to check important systems aboard Orion, including life support and deep-space communications.The crew also plans to test Orion’s ability to execute docking maneuvers for future flights in the early hours of the flight.Around the Moon and Back in 10 DaysHere's how NASA plans to send four astronauts on a trip around the moon, the first time that anyone would travel this far from Earth since the end of the Apollo program in 1972.Subscribe to The Times to read as many articles as you like.Ashley Ahn covers breaking news for The Times from New York.Kenneth Chang, a science reporter at The Times, covers NASA and the solar system, and research closer to Earth.See more on: National Aeronautics and Space AdministrationShare full articleRelated ContentAdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTSupport independent journalism with a subscription. Already a subscriber? Log in.Enjoy unlimited access for $1 a week.Welcome offer$7.50 $1/weekBilled as $4 every four weeks for your first six months, then $30 thereafter. Continue with cardPayPalCancel or pause anytime.All Access includes news, plus Games, Cooking, Audio, Wirecutter and The Athletic.Offer for a New York Times All Access subscription. Current subscribers and those who have previously accepted a sale/introductory offer from The New York Times may be ineligible for another sale/introductory offer. Subscription excludes print edition. Some games may be availabl